## Example environment file (DO NOT commit real secrets)
#
# Copy to `.env` locally if needed.
# Production should use a secret manager or CI-provided environment variables.
#
# SMS provider — must match what kk/sms_service.py implements:
#   console (dev only; blocked when APP_ENV=production)
#   otpiq   (Iraq SMS/WhatsApp — recommended)
#   twilio
#
# SMS_PROVIDER=otpiq
# OTPIQ_API_KEY=sk_live_your_otpiq_api_key
# OTPIQ_PROVIDER=sms
#
# SMS_PROVIDER=twilio
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=REPLACE_ME
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=REPLACE_ME
# TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER=REPLACE_ME

# Optional: local / docs only. On Render set OPENAI_API_KEY in the service Environment (never commit real keys).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=REPLACE_ME
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
#
# Google Play reviewer login (optional; disabled unless GOOGLE_REVIEW_LOGIN_ENABLED=1).
# Lets ONE dedicated phone number sign in with a fixed OTP that never expires and
# never sends a real SMS, so Google Play reviewers are never blocked waiting on SMS
# delivery. Applies ONLY to the exact phone number below; every other phone number's
# OTP login is completely unaffected. Never commit real values here.
# GOOGLE_REVIEW_PHONE must be EXACTLY the 10 digits typed into the app's phone
# field (no leading 0, no +964, e.g. 7999999999) -- the app always sends
# "+964" + those 10 digits, and the backend normalizes by stripping "964"
# back off, so an 11-digit "0XXXXXXXXXX" local-format value here will never
# match and will silently disable the bypass. Same 10-digit number goes into
# the Play Console "phone number" field for the reviewer.
# GOOGLE_REVIEW_LOGIN_ENABLED=1
# GOOGLE_REVIEW_PHONE=REPLACE_ME
# GOOGLE_REVIEW_OTP=REPLACE_ME
